  "blocks": {
    "\"AGENTS.md is getting huge.\"": "“AGENTS.md 变得越来越大了。”",
    "\"Most of it should be context pointers, not content. Keep the always-on rules inline; turn the deploy runbook and the style guide into skills and leave a context pointer behind.\"": "“其中大部分应该是上下文指针，而不是正文。只把始终生效的规则内联；把部署手册和样式指南做成技能，在 AGENTS.md 中留下对应的上下文指针。”",
    "A mention in one document that points to another, so the agent can pull it into the context window only when the task calls for it. The unit progressive disclosure is built from.": "上下文指针是一份文档中指向另一份文档的提示，使<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/agent\">智能体</a>只在任务需要时才把目标内容加载进<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/context-window\">上下文窗口</a>。它是构成<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/progressive-disclosure\">渐进式披露</a>的基本单元。",
    "A pointer can also tie a secondary source back to the primary source it was derived from — the compaction summary that names the original transcript, the doc that names the source file it describes. This makes the secondary source's lossiness recoverable: when the summary turns out not to be enough, the agent follows the pointer and reads the original, instead of working from whatever the summary kept.": "指针还可以把<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/secondary-source\">二手来源</a>关联回它所依据的<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/primary-source\">一手来源</a>，例如压缩摘要中注明原始对话记录，或文档中标出自己描述的源文件。这样，二手来源造成的信息损失就可以恢复：当摘要不够用时，智能体能够沿指针读取原始材料，而不是只能依赖摘要保留下来的部分继续工作。",
    "A pointer needs two parts to work: a stable path, and enough description for the agent to know when following it is worth it. A bare path is a pointer the agent has no reason to follow; \"see internal/deploy.md\" with no hint of what's inside gets skipped by a session that needed it. Write the line so it matches how tasks present: \"release, deploy, or rollback — read internal/deploy.md first\".": "一个有效指针需要两部分：稳定路径，以及足够清晰的说明，让智能体知道何时值得沿指针读取。只有路径的指针没有提供任何读取理由；如果只写“参阅 <code>internal/deploy.md</code>”，却不说明其中内容，即使会话真正需要它也可能跳过。应让描述与任务出现的方式相匹配，例如：“发布、部署或回滚——先阅读 <code>internal/deploy.md</code>”。",
    "Avoid: \"reference\" — too dry; doesn't convey that following it pulls more context in. \"Portal\" — too florid.": "<em>避免：</em>称为“reference（引用）”——过于静态，无法表达沿指针会加载更多上下文；也不要称为“portal（传送门）”——过于夸张。",
    "Pointers are everywhere once you look: lines in AGENTS.md, skill descriptions (the harness loads the description; the skill body waits behind it), filenames in a directory listing, links between docs.": "一旦开始留意，就会发现上下文指针无处不在：AGENTS.md 中的说明行、<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/skill\">技能</a>描述（运行框架先加载描述，技能正文则在其后等待按需读取）、目录列表中的文件名，以及文档之间的链接。",
    "The reason to use a pointer (instead of inlining the content) is cost. A pointer is one line in the context window. The document behind it might be thousands of tokens, but those tokens cost nothing until the agent actually follows the pointer. Inline a 2,000-token runbook in AGENTS.md and every session pays for it; replace it with \"deploy process: see internal/deploy.md\" and only the sessions that deploy ever load it. The agent follows the pointer with a tool call when the task matches.": "使用指针而不直接内联内容，原因在于成本。指针在上下文窗口中只占一行；它背后的文档可能包含数千个 <a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/token\">Token</a>，但在智能体真正沿指针读取前，这些 Token 不会产生任何成本。如果把一份 2,000 Token 的操作手册直接写进 <a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/agents-md\">AGENTS.md</a>，每次<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/session\">会话</a>都要为它付费；如果改成“部署流程：参阅 <code>internal/deploy.md</code>”，则只有执行部署任务的会话才会加载它。当任务匹配时，智能体通过一次<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/tool-call\">工具调用</a>沿着指针读取内容。",
    "Usage:": "<em>用法：</em>"
  },
